{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-61-1","title":"Psalms 61:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 David flees to God upon his former experience. 4 He vows perpetual service unto him, because of his promises.</p>\n<p>(Title.) {Neginah.}Instead of {neginath,} many MSS., have {neginoth;} and two MSS., supply {mizmor,} \"a Psalm.\" Some suppose this Psalm was composed when David was driven by Absalom's rebellion beyond Jordan, and from the sanctuary of God.</p>\n<p>4:1; 6:1; 54:1; 55:1; *titles Hear. 5:1-3; 17:1; 28:2; 55:1,2; 130:2; Php 4:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-61-2","title":"Psalms 61:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>From. 42:6; 139:9,10; De 4:29; Jon 2:2-4 my heart. 43:5; 55:5; 77:3; 142:3; 143:4; Isa 54:11; Mr 14:33,34; Lu 22:44 the rock. 18:46; 27:5; 40:2; 62:2,6; Isa 32:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-61-3","title":"Psalms 61:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>thou. 4:6,7; 116:2; 140:7; Isa 46:3,4; 2Co 1:10 strong. 18:2; Pr 18:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-61-4","title":"Psalms 61:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>abide. 7; 15:1; 23:6; 27:4; 90:1; 91:1; 92:13; Re 3:12 trust. or, make my refuge. 17:8; 57:1; 62:7; 63:7; 91:4; 142:4,5; Ru 2:12; Mt 23:37; Heb 6:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-61-5","title":"Psalms 61:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>hast heard. 56:12; 65:1; 66:19 heritage. 16:5,6; 115:13; Mal 3:16-18; Ac 10:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-61-6","title":"Psalms 61:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>wilt prolong the king's life. Heb. shalt add days to thedays of the king. 21:4,6; 72:15-17; Isa 53:10 many generations. Heb. generation and generation. 89:36,37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-61-7","title":"Psalms 61:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>abide. 41:12; Isa 9:6,7; Lu 1:33; Heb 7:21-25; 9:24 prepare. 40:11; 43:3; 57:3; Ge 24:27; 32:10; Pr 20:28; Mic 7:20; Lu 1:54,55</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-61-8","title":"Psalms 61:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>sing. 30:12; 79:13; 145:1,2; 146:2 that I. 65:1; 66:13-16</p>"}]}